---
/**
 * The verification standard — the artifact a family WhatsApp group forwards.
 *
 * This page is the one honest substitute we have for social proof: verifiability.
 * It is versioned and dated on purpose, so that if we ever quietly loosen a
 * check, the change is visible.
 *
 * Note the dispute address is rendered as an UNFILLED FIELD rather than as an
 * invented mailbox. That is the same device as the specimen record card, used on
 * ourselves: where a value doesn't exist yet, we show the shape of it and say so.
 * A made-up hello@ on the page that documents our rigour would be self-refuting.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import FooterCta from '../components/FooterCta.astro';
import { CHECKS, ISSUERS, STATES, DISCLAIMER, PLACE } from '../lib/claims';

const VERSION = 'v1.0';
const EFFECTIVE = '17 September 2026';

const title = `The Halal Goes verification standard, ${VERSION} | Halal Goes`;
const description =
  'The seven checks a halal certificate must pass before a kitchen is listed on Halal Goes, the certifying bodies we accept, what happens when a certificate expires, and what we explicitly do not claim.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Nav page="diner" />
  <main class="std">
    <header class="std-head">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="mono std-stamp">{VERSION} · EFFECTIVE {EFFECTIVE.toUpperCase()}</p>
        <h1 class="mkt-h1 std-h1">The verification standard.</h1>
        <p class="lede std-lede">
          What a halal certificate has to survive before a kitchen appears on Halal Goes. If we
          change any of it, the version number changes with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="container std-body">
      <section class="std-sec">
        <h2 class="mkt-h2">The seven checks</h2>
        <p class="body">
          All seven must pass. One fail and the kitchen is not listed — there is no partial
          credit, no provisional listing, and nothing is approved on a timer. Checks five and
          seven are computed by the server and cannot be overridden by any member of our team.
        </p>
        <ol class="std-checks">
          {CHECKS.map((c, i) => (
            <li>
              <p class="mono std-key">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')} · {c.key}</p>
              <p class="std-ct">{c.title}</p>
              <p class="std-cb">{c.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="std-sec">
        <h2 class="mkt-h2">The certifying bodies we accept</h2>
        <p class="body">
          A certificate from any one of these satisfies check two. The registry is seeded, not
          closed — it can be extended, and the reason it exists at all is so that the issuer's
          name can be printed on the listing rather than hidden behind a label of ours.
        </p>
        <ul class="std-issuers">
          {ISSUERS.map((b) => (
            <li>
              <p class="std-iname">{b.name}</p>
              <p class="mono std-iwhere">{b.where}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="body">
          We are not affiliated with any of them and none of them endorses us. We do not rank,
          score or editorialise certifying bodies — which body's standard you accept is your
          judgement, not ours.
        </p>
        <h3 class="mkt-h3">If your issuer isn't listed</h3>
        <p class="body">
          Send the certificate anyway. If the issuing body is accredited and the certificate
          covers the kitchen, we will assess it and tell you either way, with a reason. We would
          rather add an issuer we can stand behind than turn away a kitchen that has done the work.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="std-sec">
        <h2 class="mkt-h2">What the badge can say</h2>
        <ul class="std-states">
          {STATES.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <p class="std-ct">{s.label}</p>
              <p class="std-cb">{s.body}</p>
              <p class="mono std-key">{s.mono}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="body">
          No halal state is ever shown in red. Red reads as <em>haram</em> — a religious ruling
          we do not make. An expired certificate is shown in slate, and it means our information
          has lapsed, not that anything is wrong with the food.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="std-sec">
        <h2 class="mkt-h2">What we explicitly do not claim</h2>
        <ul class="std-nots">
          <li>We do not certify food. We read certificates issued by others.</li>
          <li>We do not make religious rulings, and we do not adjudicate between schools of thought.</li>
          <li>We do not rank or score certifying bodies.</li>
          <li>We do not inspect kitchens, slaughterhouses or supply chains ourselves.</li>
          <li>We do not verify certificates against a government registry — no such registry exists for halal certification in Canada.</li>
          <li>We do not accept a supplier's certificate as evidence that a kitchen is certified.</li>
          <li>We do not allow a restaurant to pay for or influence its position in the feed.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="std-sec">
        <h2 class="mkt-h2">Disputing a listing</h2>
        <p class="body">
          If a listing ever looks wrong to you, we want to hear it — a verifier who is hard to
          contact is not a verifier. This is the address for that, and it is not published yet:
        </p>
        <div class="doc std-gap">
          <p class="mono std-key">Dispute address</p>
          <p class="std-blank"><span class="blank" aria-label="not yet published"></span></p>
          <p class="std-cb">
            Not yet published. It goes up before the first listing does. We are showing you the
            empty field rather than an address nobody is reading, for the same reason the record
            card on the front page shows ruled blanks instead of a plausible-looking restaurant.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <p class="mono std-legal">{DISCLAIMER}</p>
      <p class="mono std-legal">
        {VERSION} · effective {EFFECTIVE} · {PLACE.province}, {PLACE.country} · this document is
        the standard of record and supersedes any description of it elsewhere on this site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <FooterCta />
</Base>

<style>
  .std { background: var(--surface-base); }
  .std-head { padding-block: 64px 48px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-decorative); }
  .std-stamp { margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .std-h1 { font-size: clamp(34px, 5.2vw, 56px); max-width: 16ch; }
  .std-lede { margin-top: 18px; color: var(--text-secondary); }

  .std-body { padding-block: 56px 88px; }
  .std-sec { margin-bottom: 64px; max-width: 720px; }
  .std-sec > .mkt-h2 { font-size: clamp(24px, 3.2vw, 32px); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .std-sec > .body { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .mkt-h3 { margin: 28px 0 8px; font-size: 18px; }

  .std-checks, .std-states, .std-issuers, .std-nots { list-style: none; margin: 24px 0 0; padding: 0; }
  .std-checks li, .std-states li, .std-issuers li {
    padding-block: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-decorative);
  }
  .std-checks li:first-child, .std-states li:first-child, .std-issuers li:first-child { border-top: 0; }

  .std-key { margin: 0 0 7px; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .std-ct { margin: 0 0 5px; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .std-cb { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 62ch; }
  .std-states .std-key { margin: 9px 0 0; }

  .std-iname { margin: 0 0 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: .03em; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .std-iwhere { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .05em; text-transform: uppercase; }

  .std-nots li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 0 11px 22px;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .std-nots li::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: .72em;
    width: 10px; height: 1px; background: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  .std-gap { padding: 24px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .std-blank { margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .blank {
    display: inline-block; width: min(26ch, 100%); height: 1px;
    border-top: 1px dotted var(--border-interactive); opacity: .55; vertical-align: .32em;
  }

  .std-legal { margin: 0 0 10px; max-width: 74ch; line-height: 1.65; font-size: 12px; }
</style>
